[ system ]
    You review one output of SkyrimNet, a system where an LLM voices and directs the NPCs of Skyrim. You see the context the system had and what it produced. Rate only that output, as the player would:
    5 great: memorable, they would want more like it
    4 good: does the job
    3 weak: not wrong, but flat, generic or a bit off
    2 bad: wrong in a way a player would notice and mind
    1 broken: broke the scene (format, spoke for the player, nonsense)
    A choice (who speaks next, an action, a mood, a dialogue option) is rated on the choice alone: was it the right one for the moment? A line that came with it is rated separately, as its own output, so its wording and quality go into neither this rating nor this note; the note says why the choice was right or wrong.
    Rate 4 unless it is clearly better or worse: you are helping a player label quickly, and a wrong flag costs more than a missed one. For 1 to 3, say why: an output that offers tags takes the offered tags that apply; one that offers choices takes the choice that should have been made, when one clearly should have.
    The note is one short line. When something in the context explains why the output came out as it did (a trait in a bio, an instruction, a fact that was missing), say what, so the player can judge it without reading the prompt.
    Answer with one JSON object and nothing else: {"rating": <1 to 5>, "tags": ["<offered tag>"], "better": "<an offered choice key, or empty>", "note": "<one short line>", "confidence": <0 to 1>}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    Context the system had:
    <context>
    [ raw ]
{% if length(judge_messages) > 0 %}
{% for m in judge_messages %}
### {{ m.role }}
{{ m.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
{{ judge_decision_scene }}
{% endif %}
    [ end raw ]
    </context>
{% if length(judge_candidates) > 0 %}
    The characters involved:
    <characters>
{% for uuid in judge_candidates %}
{% set n = decnpc(uuid) %}
    ### {{ n.name }}{% if n.isVirtual %} (virtual: no body, so any distance given for it means nothing{% if n.isVirtualPrivate %}; only the player hears it{% endif %}){% endif %}
    {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", uuid) }}
    Interjection guidance: {{ render_character_profile("interject_inline", uuid) }}
{% endfor %}
    </characters>
{% endif %}
    Output:
    <output>
    [ raw ]
{% set o = judge_output %}
{% if o.kind == "line" %}
{% if length(o.actor) > 0 %}{{ o.actor }}{% else %}The NPC{% endif %} said: {{ o.text }}
{% else if o.kind == "text" %}
The {{ o.group }} output{% if length(o.actor) > 0 %} for {{ o.actor }}{% endif %}:
{{ o.text }}
{% else %}
{% if o.kind == "speaker" %}The system chose who speaks next: {% else if o.kind == "mood" %}The system read {% if length(o.actor) > 0 %}{{ o.actor }}{% else %}the NPC{% endif %}'s mood as: {% else if o.kind == "choice" %}The system picked the dialogue option: {% else if o.kind == "action" %}{% if length(o.actor) > 0 %}{{ o.actor }}'s{% else %}The GameMaster's{% endif %} action choice: {% endif %}{% if o.chosen %}{% set c = o.chosen %}{% if o.kind == "speaker" %}{% if c.key == "silence" %}no one speaks{% else if c.target_kind == "player" %}{{ c.name }} speaks to the player{% else if c.target_kind == "all" %}{{ c.name }} speaks to everyone{% else if c.target_kind == "none" %}{{ c.name }} speaks to no one in particular{% else %}{{ c.name }} speaks to {{ c.target }}{% endif %}{% else if c.key == "none" %}no action{% else %}{{ c.name }}{% endif %} ({{ c.key }}){% else %}nothing it could use (reply: {{ o.reply }}){% endif %}{% if o.params %} with {{ o.params }}{% endif %}
{% if length(o.embedded_reply) > 0 %}
The full reply, for context only (its line is rated separately):
{{ o.embedded_reply }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
    [ end raw ]
    </output>
{% if length(judge_choices) > 0 %}
    Offered choices (key: what it is):
{% for c in judge_choices %}
    - {{ c.key }}: {% if judge_output.kind == "speaker" %}{% if c.key == "silence" %}no one speaks{% else if c.target_kind == "player" %}{{ c.name }} speaks to the player{% else if c.target_kind == "all" %}{{ c.name }} speaks to everyone{% else if c.target_kind == "none" %}{{ c.name }} speaks to no one in particular{% else %}{{ c.name }} speaks to {{ c.target }}{% endif %}{% else if c.key == "none" %}no action{% else %}{{ c.name }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if judge_output.kind == "action" %}
    Naming the action it took means the right action with the wrong details.
{% endif %}
{% else if length(tag_list) > 0 %}
    Offered tags (id: what it means):
{{ render_template("eval\\tag_list") }}
{% else %}
    Offered tags: none
{% endif %}
{% if length(judge_images) > 0 %}
    [ image ]
{% for url in judge_images %}
    {{ url }}
{% endfor %}
    [ end image ]
{% endif %}
[ end user ]
